---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<Base title="Pricing" description="Lumo is free. You bring your own model provider API key and pay the provider directly for what you use. No subscription, no markup.">
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Pricing"
    title="Lumo is free."
    lede="There is no subscription and no Lumo account. You connect your own model provider key and pay the provider directly, at their prices, for what you use."
  />
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <section class="panel price-card" aria-labelledby="p-lumo">
        <p class="eyebrow">Lumo</p>
        <h2 class="h-display" id="p-lumo">$0</h2>
        <p>The app, every feature as it ships, and updates.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><span>No account to create</span></li>
          <li><span>No subscription or trial period</span></li>
          <li><span>No markup on model usage: Lumo never sits between you and the provider’s bill</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="panel price-card" aria-labelledby="p-provider">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your model provider</p>
        <h2 class="h-display" id="p-provider">Pay as you go</h2>
        <p>
          Lumo uses Claude models through your own Anthropic API key. Anthropic bills you directly based on usage. See
          <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/pricing">Anthropic’s pricing</a> for current rates.
        </p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><span>Choose which Claude model Lumo uses; smaller models cost less</span></li>
          <li><span>Each task has a spend limit, so a runaway task stops</span></li>
          <li><span>Set budgets and alerts in your provider’s console</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h-display" id="faq-title">Questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose faq">
        <h3>Why do I need my own API key?</h3>
        <p>
          Lumo has no cloud service of its own. Your requests go straight from your computer to the provider you chose, which keeps your data out of
          one more company’s servers and keeps the app free.
        </p>
        <h3>Do purchases made through Lumo cost extra?</h3>
        <p>
          No. When Lumo helps you order food or shop, it hands you off to the provider or merchant, and you pay them at their normal prices. Lumo
          takes no fee and does not handle payment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
